   371	It was soft at the folds by now. It had come up a bluff in a post-room sort in the year's seventh week, and he had read it some dozens of times, at a sill, and knew it without the flame. A Gold at Auremont had written to tell him not to mistake what was happening to him for procedure. She had said that the rematch stood, and she had told him to keep himself unclassified.
