  “Good room.”
- The closings, four call days, district-station girl, Ilsev/Havel windows, five ruling heads,
  three roads, priced departures, last-bout exchanges, verdict order, boards ritual, nondisclosure,
  first pull, unused Anchor, and forms on Bracken's counter are plan-required facts or events. They
  are excluded where the manuscript supplies new scene construction, causality, physical business,
  or beat order.
- Recurring gestures such as hands flat on a table, looking at a paper, squaring a leaf, and a room
  going quiet were treated as common prose unless they carried the source sentence's substantive
  sequence.

## Dense-scene remedies

None. No scene contains more than one genuine tracked passage. Chapter 49 scene 3 and Chapter 54
scene 3 each have one line-level repair candidate; neither needs a new entry point or reordered
scene on source-distance grounds. The protected Tier B convergence in Chapter 54 scenes 5–6 is
reported above but does not make those scenes densely tracked under the requested counting rules.

