editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:242:B5 canon: the rule is written by Karis, copied into Hesk's book "under the minute from two nights before", ch59:103: *The conditions may complete themselves anywhere; the deciding may not. The line holds: directed, open-eyed — and from tonight, costed. Never again in the middle of a fight unless what follows has been priced first, at the weight it will come at. Yesterday the bill fell due with the one person on the floor who could have made it worse choosing not to. We don't get to plan on that twice.* Four initials, ch59:107 (Karis, Brom, Lira, Cael, in that order); "Now it's the house's." The M9 ruling names the gap it repairs: rule three held "on paper as far as paper went" (ch60:23). Note for A12: "directed, open-eyed" is now ON THE PAGE in B5 as the costed rule's own words (ch59:103), so B6 may recall it as B5's wording; it is still never B4's.
