editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:249:B5 canon: the first waystation on the road home, "He came down the room and sat on the bench, in the middle of it, between Lira's boots and Karis's lamp, at the table." and "every night, at every board, every one of them counted him" (ch60:87–95); the manifest "written out the evening before the closing", eleven names, *records and floor scheduling* against his own "in his own small upright hand" (ch60:97); the T25 report verbatim (ch58:103) and the closing word left off — the page never names the word ("the one word that closed it … He held the pen over the space and did not write the word", ch58:105–107); the ledger names it *Routine.* SL:81 and BM:51 ("at the middle of the bench since the road home") hold. One note for the author, no plan change: B6 has Seln go on filing "true, empty reports" in "the old pattern" until the year's close (BM:135–137; M5:20; M7:40) — B5 made leaving the closing word off a one-time act of a report that "did not need building". Default for B6: at Halcenvane he builds again and the old pattern (closing word included) comes back; M9's unfiled road draft is the second report of his life he did not need to build. Say it once if the author wants it; otherwise leave the word off the page as B5 did.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:274:B5 canon: the second return, verbatim, *Referral closed at registry level; no further inquiry authorized.* (ch58:21; read upside down by Havel and copied at the head of his fifth, ch58:49); the M9 ruling fixes the chain to B4 — the first referral went up from Greyvane and came down twice with "no originating authority of record"; the second, fuller one, filed at Halcenvane on the fifteenth of Reaping a level higher, is the one now closed. Her private sheet: stationer's paper from the coopers' row, "in the hand she had used as a girl at her mother's table", folded into her coat (ch58:35); Havel sees only the paper's kind. Havel's fifth: written "in his narrow room at the inn behind the east tower", put "in with the other four between the manuals" (ch58:47–51) — the edition renders B4's notebook as loose sheets between the second and third manuals in his kit (M9 ruling). B6's "five entries" at entry is confirmed; the sixth (M5) and "stops at six" (BM:498, M7:38) stand.
