editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:284:B5 canon: not drafted; "No optional Norhold session (C8): two renewals on paper at the book's close (Book 6 audit A11 → owner)" (M9 ruling); the author's note (j): "the two days at Norhold after the match hold a destabilized fighter".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:287:B5 canon: "Rematch," she said. (ch59:183, the closing — protected item 57); "Find out what you are. Then find me. I want the rematch with whatever that is." (ch56:226, on the stone); "That was mine," — "A piece of it," said Cael. (ch56:210–216: the line is Cael's answer, "the truest thing he could give her without giving her the rest"); then hers: "Nineteen years. Nobody has ever shown me something I couldn't name." (ch56:222); her notebook line *Today somebody asked me something.* (ch57); her citation sealed in her case lining, unread; she "did not try to work out how he had done it". SL:88 ("An appointment, not a challenge.") holds. B6's statement ("Never. Not at Gold.", M3:69) and letter are B6's own and build on these; the reply at the Line (M9) answers the letter. Daeva nineteen; Gold Rank Three (ch54:99).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:303:B5 canon (ch60:195–211): item 59 every clause as mapped; "Years ago," said Brom. (ch60:205); Karis "Noted."; Seln on the tailboard, silent; the closing paragraph with "a room with no windows". SL:79 holds; B6 never quotes the lines (no hit in BM/SL/M1–M9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:307:**The count after B5 M9.** On paper at B6's entry: the Greyvane grant and **two** renewals — the twentieth of Reaping (B4; B5 ch1:125 "one semester stamp, renewed") and the mill town (B5 M2). The half-year sitting that the cadence put at Norhold did not sit (M9 ruling; author note (j)); the next by cadence falls about the first term's close in B6 (M5), not in the interval. So the applied PENDING notes (BM:22, BM:584, SL:30, M1:35 item 10), which said "at most three", are now "two", and nothing in B5 can supply the pole's "four".
