editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:330:- **Vastin's nineteen years in his room.** B5 canon: "The room was high up in the Compact's house, two days from Norhold by the post road. He had worked in it for nineteen years." — the paved court, the porter feeding pigeons, the long cabinet of shallow drawers, the seal-press "screwed to the desk's corner himself, crooked", three trays *in, held, done* (ch50:115; also ch5:9, ch29:215); his left hand "had begun some years ago to dislike mornings" (ch5:9) — "worse in the evenings now as well as the mornings" (ch58:241); a stiff left hand is new canon (M9 ruling). B6's Vastin windows (M3, M6, M7, M9) sit in "the western administration" (M3:13) with no room described.
